{
 "_meta": {
  "title": "Kernel words for the reduced Burau representation of B4 at rational specializations t = p/q",
  "date": "2026-06-11",
  "construction": "Work in Birman's free subgroup F2 = <X, Y> of B4 (X = s3 s1^-1, Y = s2 s3 s1^-1 s2^-1). The element u = x Y X y is lower triangular over Z[t,t^-1] with diagonal (t^4, t^-2, t^-2); its Levi 2x2 block is the central matrix t^-2 I. Hence for any word p whose Burau matrix at t has first row proportional to e1^T ('parabolic'), v = [p, u] lies in the abelian unipotent group N = I + (a e2 + b e3) e1^T, where conjugation by u^-1 is multiplication by t^6 and v^k = I + k(v - I). At t = p/q this gives the exact relation u^-1 v^{q^6} u = v^{p^6}, so R = u^-1 v^{q^6} u v^{-p^6} is a nontrivial element of F2 (conjugate powers in a free group have equal exponents) in the kernel of Burau at t. Parabolic words are found by exact projective collisions of first rows. All verifications use exact rational arithmetic.",
  "scripts": [
   "rationalKernelSearch.py",
   "symbolicParabolicSweep.py",
   "padicTriBeam.py"
  ],
  "headline_results": [
   "t=2: kernel words confirmed; new shorter unipotent v of length 36 (previous v = w2 u^-1 had length 96); explicit kernel word u^-1 v u v^-64 of length 2340 verified exactly.",
   "t=1/2: mirror of t=2 under the t <-> 1/t symmetry; u^-1 v^64 u = v.",
   "Among all 84 rationals p/q with |p|,q <= 8 (t != 0,+-1), ONLY t = 2 and t = 1/2 admit parabolic words with both collision constituents of length <= 11 (p of length <= 22).",
   "Symbolic sweep of all 1,062,880 reduced words of length <= 12: no word is parabolic at any rational t outside {0,+-1} (no linear factors at all). 145,184 words are parabolic at algebraic points, dominated by the cyclotomic factor t^2-t+1 (zeta_6, 118,042 events) where t^6=1 makes the relation degenerate; non-cyclotomic algebraic specializations reachable at length <= 12 include roots of t^2+t-1, t^3-t^2+1, t^4+t-1, and many quintics/sextics.",
   "t=3 deep scan: no parabolic words from collision constituents of length <= 15 (p of length <= 30).",
   "The only words whose first row is proportional to e1^T identically in t (length <= 12) are the powers of u itself.",
   "The 62-letter t=2 'relation' produced by the float beam search (formerly in relation_db.json drafts) is NOT a relation in exact arithmetic; the 92-letter w2 relation IS exact."
  ],
  "exponent_pattern": "The Baumslag-Solitar exponent is always t^6 = p^6/q^6, forced by diag(u) = (t^4, t^-2, t^-2): 64 = 2^6 at t=2. Conjugating by u^k gives t^{6k}."
 },
